      "message": "Review Summary — Change 94950\nVerdict: :large_yellow_circle: Comment — nearly ready, one medium-severity fix recommended.\nWhat the change does: Adds one new test case Verify Privilege Change When LDAP Is Unreachable and its orchestrator keyword Change User Privilege When LDAP Unreachable to redfish/account_service/test_ldap_configuration.robot. The test validates that a local admin can change the privilege of a user originally created by an LDAP admin when LDAP is unreachable — a meaningfully distinct scenario from the existing Verify Privilege Change By Local Admin When LDAP Is Unreachable test.\nQuick Stats: 0 High | 1 Medium | 1 Low | 0 Unresolved threads\nIssues Found\n#SeverityIssue1:large_yellow_circle: MediumTest [Teardown] lacks session guard — the teardown at line 901 calls Create LDAP Configuration without first ensuring a valid Redfish session. If the FINALLY block\u0027s Redfish.Login fails, the teardown will run unauthenticated. Fix: prepend Run Keyword And Ignore Error Redfish.Login AND to the teardown chain (matches the suite-wide pattern on line 13).2:large_green_circle: LowCommit message keyword name mismatch — the commit body says \u0027Privilege Change When LDAP Unreachable\u0027; the actual keyword is Change User Privilege When LDAP Unreachable.",
